.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-gpg-cat 1  "git-gpg-cat " 
.SH NAME
git\-gpg\-cat \- Cat \- decrypt a single tracked file to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-gpg cat\fR [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-gpg\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cat \- decrypt a single tracked file to stdout
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Your email address
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-gpg\-home\fR \fI<GPG_HOME>\fR
Key store directory (default: $HOME/.git\-gpg)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR
Read the passphrase for a passphrase\-protected private key from stdin (exactly one line). Wins over the GITGPG_PASSPHRASE environment variable; never pass a passphrase as a CLI argument
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
File to decrypt
